From 1c1d26ce568b052e8bc3ea0769f06e572789c976 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 04:57:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(quote-check): compare the quotes a homeowner is already
 holding, and price nothing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The highest-intent moment in this business is a homeowner holding three quotes
that are thousands of dollars apart. Every flooring company in this city
competes for that moment with review counts, and a review count does not tell
anyone which of three numbers is correct.

Usually none of them is wrong. They are pricing different work: one includes
subfloor preparation, disposal of the existing floor and four coats, another
does not, and nothing on either document says so. /quote-check puts two to four
quotes side by side against 22 line items and reports whether the totals can be
compared at all. Fourteen of the items are ones this business already publishes
as belonging in a hardwood quote, each linking to the page that published it;
the rest are neutral scope questions — who moves the furniture, who takes the
old floor away — where including the item is not better, it is a different job.

It runs entirely in the browser. There is no fetch in the component: the visitor
is holding other companies' commercial documents, and a tool that uploads them
is not usable by the people who most need it.

WHAT IT REFUSES TO DO, AND WHY THAT IS ENFORCED BY A GUARD

The obvious improvement is to price the gaps — "Quote B omits subfloor prep,
typically $1.80/sq ft". That converts a scope comparison into a performance
claim about a market. Competition Act s.74.01(1)(b) requires adequate and proper
testing to exist BEFORE the claim; no such test exists for a typical GTA
line-item price and none can be assembled from published data. Since Bill C-59
the exposure is the greater of CAD 10M or 3% of worldwide gross revenue, and
since 20 June 2025 a private party can bring it to the Tribunal directly.
Characterising a competitor's document additionally invites the analysis in
Energizer Brands v Gillette 2023 FC 804.

That edit will arrive months from now, looking small and reasonable, from
someone who has read none of the above. So scripts/verify-quote-check.mjs fails
the build on a dollar figure or a percentage in anything rendered, on evaluative
vocabulary about quotes or companies, on an exported function whose name prices
or ranks, on a 'published' item whose citation does not resolve to a page this
repository generates, and on a 'scope' item that quietly acquires a citation.
Regression-tested against all five.

TWO GUARDS WERE BLIND AND ARE NOT NOW

verify:a11y matched element attributes with [^>]*?, which stops at the first ">"
— and an arrow function in a handler contains one. Every attribute after
onChange={() => …} was invisible, so correctly labelled controls were reported
as unnamed and the fix a developer reaches for is to reorder attributes, which
teaches nothing and leaves the trap set.

verify:navigation read chrome links only as href="/x" in markup. The header's
mega-menus are data — { label, href } — so for the reachability graph the entire
header menu did not exist. It now counts 41 chrome links where it counted one; a
page linked only from the menu was previously indistinguishable from a page
linked from nowhere, which is the exact distinction that guard exists to make.

Also: /api/v1/quote-check with the checklist as data and its refusals stated in
the payload, an OpenAPI schema, a contract test, 16 unit tests, header and
sitemap entries, an llms.txt entry, and a link from /pricing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
